docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:128:3. **Independent artifact approval: pending.** The manifest remains `pending_independent_review`. Only hashes of changed framework files and the necessary new authority-module entry are updated. Hash equality is not approval; independent approval must be separately recorded.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:136:Offline validation uses temporary records, fake clocks/connections, and guarded credential/database interfaces; it includes concurrency, negative paths, durable/exclusive writes, denial persistence, expiry/retention, artifact/prerequisite separation, direct/Alembic bypass checks, acknowledged and uncertain commit outcomes, and recovery blocking. Deterministic autonomy review finds no AI in ordinary authorization, expiry, audit, execution, or recovery decisions. Owner review, issuance, and reconciliation remain explicit administrative controls. Offline tests do not establish live operational or production readiness; independent artifact review and a later separately authorized testing-only baseline validation are still required.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:250:Establish and owner-approve the precise audit destination, retention policy, failed-write behavior, and operational evidence procedure before migration execution is authorized. Follow the sanitized evidence categories, exclusions, independent review, and same-account log limitations in `WORKFLOW.md`. Raw operational logs stay outside Git; only independently reviewed, sanitized validation evidence may accompany an authorized Git checkpoint. Audit persistence is not implemented; no retention period or new paid logging service is approved.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:252:**Deterministic autonomy review: design PASS; implementation and operational behavior awaiting validation.** The lifecycle covers explicit identities, artifact approval, one-revision transactions, ownership, search path, locks/timeouts, drift/grant checks, rollback, uncertain commits, repeat execution, and evidence. Administrative bootstrap, approval decisions, and exceptional recovery remain justified administrative boundaries. PostgreSQL behavior and negative/recovery paths require future validation; neither catalog inspection nor Stage 1 documentation proves operational or production readiness.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:265:| 6 | Independent security review | Requires separate authorization; assess effective authority, isolation, secrets, artifacts, execution, and evidence/recovery controls. |
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:283:- Runtime grants are exactly SELECT/INSERT on the notification table and UPDATE on its `unsubscribed_at` column. Generated feature types remain private. Extend exact catalog/constraint/index/dependency/ACL validation, manifest inventory and audit state vocabulary for 0003 while preserving all Stage 5 review, testing-before-development, single-revision transaction, authorization, lock and recovery controls. The manifest stays `pending_independent_review`.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:285:- Deterministic autonomy review: **source/offline PASS**. Eligibility, normalization, preference/state validation, consent, duplicate suppression, receipt/signature checks, withdrawal and repeat handling use fixed rules. Negative/failure/recovery paths are tested. No ordinary operation requires AI or per-submission administrative review. Artifact approval, separately authorized migrations, public deployment and future announcement/delivery governance remain explicit administrative boundaries.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:286:- Next database checkpoint: independent review of exact 0003 artifacts/prerequisites, then a separate owner-authorized **TESTING** `0002_state_requests -> 0003_notifications` validation. Verify real PostgreSQL partial-index races, constraints, dependency/type ACL and column-grant semantics, runtime identity, persistence, rollback/uncertain outcomes and real API/browser behavior. DEVELOPMENT requires successful TESTING evidence for matching artifacts and its own authorization. No live readiness is claimed by offline success.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:295:- Extend the manifest, exact catalog definitions/dependencies, private feature type ACLs, explicit matching-runtime SELECT/INSERT grants, and authorization evidence state vocabulary only as required for 0002. Preserve the Stage 5 single-revision transaction, independent review, owner issuance, testing-before-development, lock/session identity, audit and recovery controls. The manifest remains `pending_independent_review`.
docs\WEBSITE_PLAN.md:297:- Live functionality remains unvalidated. Next checkpoint: independent review of the exact 0002 artifacts and prerequisites, followed by a separate owner-issued **testing** authorization for `0001_migration_baseline -> 0002_state_requests`. Successful authorized PostgreSQL/API/browser validation precedes separate development authorization.
