logs\codex-20261027T2127578409649Z-eb726ef7ffb94f0aacac154f8412ff41.log:7509:Offline validation uses temporary records, fake clocks/connections, and guarded credential/database interfaces; it includes concurrency, negative paths, durable/exclusive writes, denial persistence, expiry/retention, artifact/prerequisite separation, direct/Alembic bypass checks, acknowledged and uncertain commit outcomes, and recovery blocking. Deterministic autonomy review finds no AI in ordinary authorization, expiry, audit, execution, or recovery decisions. Owner review, issuance, and reconciliation remain explicit administrative controls. Offline tests do not establish live operational or production readiness; independent artifact review and a later separately authorized testing-only baseline validation are still required.
