2696:The only new transition is `0002_state_requests -> 0003_notifications`; a later separately authorized no-op may start at 0003. Preserve revisions 0001/0002 byte-for-byte. No base/0001 jump to 0003, multi-revision upgrade, downgrade or stamp is supported. Exact-artifact independent approval remains pending; changed hashes are integrity evidence only and do not reuse prior approvals or execution authorizations.
2700:Signup requires strict JSON fields `email`, `web_launch`, `android_launch`, `ios_launch`, `state` (null or a registered code), `consent=true` and a fresh 32-byte browser-generated hex receipt `token`. The server validates every field and stores only the receipt hash. Repeated active email submissions never overwrite preferences or consent; receipt replays never reactivate withdrawn records. Responses disclose no subscriber existence or existing preferences. The returned signed capability controls only a lifecycle created by that receipt; a duplicate from another receipt cannot yield the original link. The page explains this and tells visitors to save the private link.
2702:Unsubscribe links use `/gramanna.html#unsubscribe=<hash>.<signature>`. Fragments stay out of HTTP paths/query logs, are removed from the address bar immediately, and require explicit user action. POST the signed token with the same origin and browser CSRF protections. No email address is needed to withdraw; invalid signatures cannot mutate, and successful repeated/unknown valid receipts produce a generic confirmation. Future approved delivery can recreate links with `UnsubscribeCapabilities.issue(stored_digest)` using the same protected key. No email delivery/verification is implemented or claimed.
